The user reported that `service.make_user(1, 'Ada', 'ada@example.com')` raises `ValueError: Protocol message User has no "email" field.`

After investigating the code and the generated files, I found the discrepancy in the protocol buffer definition. In `proto/acct/v1/user.proto`, the field for the user's email is defined as `emial` (with a typo) instead of `email`.

```protobuf
message User {
  int64 id = 1;
  string name = 2;
  string emial = 3; // <-- TYPO HERE
  Role role = 4;
}
```

This typo is what causes the runtime error `User has no "email" field.` when Python code attempts to access or set the `email` attribute.

The fix is to correct the typo in `proto/acct/v1/user.proto` from `emial` to `email`. Since this is a generated file, I need to modify the `.proto` file and then assume a rebuild/re-run of tests will use the corrected definition.

I will now update the file.

